From: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom_q6v5_wcss_sec: leave the coredump off by
 default

With RPROC_COREDUMP_INLINE the recovery of a crashed Q6 waits for
somebody to read the dump from /sys/class/devcoredump, and gives up only
when devcoredump times out after five minutes. Nothing reads it on a
router, so every firmware crash costs five minutes of dead radios before
the restart is even tried. Default to no dump; it can be had with

  echo inline > /sys/class/remoteproc/remoteproc0/coredump

Signed-off-by: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>

--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_wcss_sec.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_wcss_sec.c
@@ -462,7 +462,7 @@ static int wcss_sec_probe(struct platfor
 	qcom_add_ssr_subdev(rproc, &wcss->ssr_subdev, desc->ss_name);
 
 	rproc->auto_boot = false;
-	rproc->dump_conf = RPROC_COREDUMP_INLINE;
+	rproc->dump_conf = RPROC_COREDUMP_DISABLED;
 	rproc_coredump_set_elf_info(rproc, ELFCLASS32, EM_NONE);
 
 	if (desc->use_tmelcom) {
